{
    "background_story": "Iyla was a majestic aoudad, roaming the rugged Atlas Mountains with her herd. Her broad, spiral horns and shaggy coat made her a striking figure against the rocky terrain. Iyla's name, meaning 'halo of light' in the local dialect, suited her well, as she seemed to radiate a gentle aura. Despite the harsh climate, she thrived, scaling sheer cliffs and navigating treacherous paths with ease. Iyla's sure-footedness and agility allowed her to reach the most inaccessible peaks, where she would graze on the sweetest grasses. Her calm demeanor and gentle nature made her a leader among her peers, and her herd relied on her to guide them through the harshest of winters. Iyla's strength and resilience inspired awe in all who laid eyes on her.",
